I was hanging out with the cool kids in rec.games.roguelike.nethack when 
Cuboidz got out a spraycan and scrawled the following:
>  I'm pretty new to Nethack, and I've come to dislike shops because of
>  all the drudgery involved in putting them to good use: price-ID'ing
>  scrolls, stealing stuff with your pet ...
> 
>  So I'm wondering whether it is feasible to just use shops for shopping
>  only? And in the same vein: what do you (usually) do when you
>  encounter a shop?

I do the following price-IDing:

scroll of identify
spellbooks (after checking BUC with a pet/altar)
lamps (if I've not already found one that's run out of oil)
weapons, to find the most enchanted sword/dagger

I don't bother with the kind of price-ID that requires me to
memorise/look up the relative costs of items.  I can remember that
?ofIdentify is the cheapest and that's all.

I'll try on interesting armour after confirming it's not cursed, and
if it doesn't self-identify (water-walking boots, unenchanted gauntlets
of dexterity or helm of brilliance), I'll probably buy it anyway as it's
not that expensive and could turn out useful.  I'll buy the required
candles and every magic marker, and other tools (such as keys, towels,
bags, tinning kits, magic whistles, musical instrument) if I've not
already found one. 

In some extreme cases, I might buy a few food rations.  [S] has frozen
food stores which I'll use to stock up on intrinsics, and scoff every
newt corpse in hope of the mild buzz.

I'll only use the pet to shoplift if there's an artifact involved.  I
might also come back to shops in the main dungeon once I've got lots of
zorkmids and have identified all the interesting stuff, in case of a
useful but rare item (wand of death, scroll of charging, potentially
needed ring).


